{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>The door</b> — the tav is root, like the tav of קשת, or the tav in place of heh." "<b>Turns</b> — linked to the verse, front and back." "<b>Upon its hinge</b> — from the Aramaic translation תרתין צירין, which are the doors, and likewise the meaning is: the door turns upon its hinge in closing and in opening, and so the sluggard turns upon his bed from side to side and does not rise to seek his sustenance; therefore after it he buried [it]." "<b>Another interpretation: the door turns</b> — when the doors are opened for each man to go out to his work, and the sluggard is still upon his bed."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:24:53.050135305Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}